# Next.js Development Rules (Next.js 15/16 + React 19)

## Latest Updates (2025)

### Next.js 16 Features
- **Turbopack Stable**: Now default bundler with 10× faster Fast Refresh
- **Cache Components**: Opt-in caching with `use cache` directive
- **React 19.2**: View Transitions, useEffectEvent, and latest React features
- **Layout Deduplication**: Optimized prefetching for shared layouts
- **Build Adapters API**: Custom build integrations and deployment adapters

### Next.js 15 Features
- **React 19 Support**: Full React 19 integration in App Router
- **No Default Caching**: fetch, GET routes, and navigations uncached by default
- **Turbopack Dev**: Stable development mode with improved performance
- **React Compiler**: Experimental support for automatic memoization
- **unstable_after**: Execute code after response finishes
- **Enhanced Forms**: Client-side navigation with next/form
- **TypeScript Config**: next.config.ts support

## App Router Structure

### File-based Routing
```
app/
├── globals.css
├── layout.tsx          # Root layout
├── page.tsx           # Home page
├── loading.tsx        # Loading UI
├── error.tsx          # Error UI
├── not-found.tsx      # 404 page
├── dashboard/
│   ├── layout.tsx     # Nested layout
│   ├── page.tsx       # /dashboard
│   ├── settings/
│   │   └── page.tsx   # /dashboard/settings
│   └── [id]/
│       └── page.tsx   # /dashboard/[id]
└── api/
    └── users/
        └── route.ts   # API endpoints
```

